# CLAUDE.md

> Default language for this project: English

## Project Overview

{{PROJECT_OVERVIEW}}

## Documentation Rules

> Rule of thumb: stable material that a second task will reuse goes to `.docs/`; anything that only serves one work episode goes to `.project/`.

- **`.docs/` shared material**: environment and access details, feature lists, API/reporting specs, resource inventories, acceptance and test reports
- **`.project/` workspace**: requirement discussions, designs, demo and verification runs, debugging, Q&A records, plans and retrospectives
- `.docs/` groups material into numbered category directories: `01-environments/` (fixed), `02-feature-list/`, `03-data-reporting/`; `00-` reserved for overview; **no `YYYYMMDD-` date directories** — append new categories, never renumber or reuse
- `.docs/README.md` is the shared-material index; keep each document and its attachments in one place, link from `.project/` topics, keep only the latest version
- **One topic, one directory** as `.project/YYYYMMDD-<topic>/`; use numbered subdirectories such as `01-discussion` for steps
- {{OTHER_DOCUMENTATION_REQUIREMENTS}}

## Environment Index

> Create files only for environments that exist; drop the rows for missing ones instead of inventing access details.

| Environment | Access | Details |
|-------------|--------|---------|
| Test | {{TEST_ENV_ACCESS}} | `.docs/01-environments/test.md` |
| Staging | {{UAT_ENV_ACCESS}} | `.docs/01-environments/uat.md` |
| Production | {{PROD_ENV_ACCESS}} | `.docs/01-environments/prd.md` |

## Task Tracking

> One register, one detail location: the root `TODO.md` is the index and `.project/` holds the details.

- For a new task, create `.project/YYYYMMDD-<topic>/` and name the body after the topic
- Merge follow-up work on the same topic into the existing topic directory (use numbered subdirectories such as `01-discussion` for steps); do not create a second topic directory
- Add one line under "In Progress" in the root `TODO.md`: `### <item>, see [<directory>](.project/<directory>)`
- When done, move the item from "In Progress" to "Completed / Archived" with a `### ✅` prefix

## Development Rules
- Read `TODO.md` and `CHANGELOG.md` before starting work to catch up on project progress
- Add comments to file headers, core functions, and business logic; use type annotations consistently
- Record any open discussion items in `TODO.md` when work is finished

## Commit Rules
- Do not commit intermediate artifacts, auxiliary documents, or development plans
- Decide whether a change is user-visible and record it in `CHANGELOG.md`; that file covers functional changes only, never implementation details

## Other
- Add dependency, testing, and deployment rules as the project evolves; this file must not exceed 50 lines
- Put long development guides in `.project/` and link to them here, e.g. [Release Notes Guide](.project/release-note.md)
